<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Californios</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Californios were the Hispanic, mostly mestizo, inhabitants of Alta <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a> under Spanish and Mexican rule. After the secularisation of the missions in the 1830s many became ranchers on large land grants, trading hides and tallow with American ships. After the American conquest of 1846–1848 many lost their lands through legal challenges and debt.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/californios.jpg" alt="Californios" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original: Donald Graeme Kelley Vectorization: Devin Cook · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_California.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
